## Actions

# The account's workspaces, keys, usage, model and webhooks, as the API publishes them.
tilo-account-workspaces-list = Your workspaces, whether this device keeps each, and the hosts you can create on; with labels, those labelled so
tilo-account-workspaces-create = Create a workspace; the host may refuse (quota, payment)
tilo-account-workspaces-branch = Branch a workspace of yours: a new one of yours that starts as its copy and goes on apart
tilo-account-workspaces-rename = Name a workspace, for every list and device of it; its owners and moderators may
tilo-account-workspaces-delete = Delete a workspace of yours and everything in it, for good; its keys are revoked
tilo-account-workspaces-enter = Keep a workspace of yours on this device, synced with its host
tilo-account-workspaces-leave = Stop keeping a workspace on this device; you stay in it
tilo-account-workspaces-join = Join a workspace, by the invitation that brings you in or through its open entry, and keep it on this device
tilo-account-workspaces-unattended = Let keys made for one workspace alone run commands in its machine without asking each time (asks you first), or ask again
tilo-account-workspaces-import = Take in, once, the workspaces and keys this computer's desktop kept itself
tilo-account-keys-create = Ask the person for a new key; it waits for them
tilo-account-keys-mint = A key for one workspace, for an agent there
tilo-account-keys-key-revoke = Revoke this key and every key it minted
tilo-account-usage-read = What your workspaces keep and ran, and your plan
tilo-account-models-ask = Ask your own model one turn; the invocation's newest item keeps its answer so far
tilo-account-webhooks-list = This key's webhooks, with the key their deliveries are signed with; with workspace, that workspace's
tilo-account-webhooks-create = Post a workspace's events to a URL, signed by the device that keeps it; answers the key it signs with
tilo-account-webhooks-delete = Stop posting to a webhook of this key
